WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.060
In my initial video, I mostly talked about
The Shape of Water being a Hellboy spinoff

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.460
or a Creature from the Black Lagoon sequel.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.270
There were all kinds of other ideas being
presented, and I love seeing those intelligent

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:18.580
discussions taking place in my comments, so
here are some of those theories.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:23.770
Many of you were reminded of HP Lovecraft’s
creation, The Deep Ones, from Dagon and Shadow

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:24.770
Over Innsmouth.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:29.591
I’m not much of a Lovecraft expert, so I
looked it up on HP Lovecraft Wiki, which said

00:00:29.591 --> 00:00:33.470
basically said that they are ocean-dwelling
humanoid fish people with an affinity for

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:34.950
mating with humans.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:39.680
Some of their physical traits include small
ears, glassy bulging eyes, hairless heads,

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.350
webbed fingers, folds on the neck which become
gills and rigid scales on the back.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.480
Knowing that, I’d say that there’s a very
good chance that Del Toro was inspired by

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.730
Lovecraft on this one, but the question becomes,
was he inspired directly?

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:56.540
There’s been a bit of controversy about
The Shape of Water in the indie film world

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.400
because of how similar the movie seems to
be to this 2015 short film, The Space Between

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.500
Us, with many of you making accusations of
plagiarism, saying he took the concept, the

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.109
themes, and the look directly from The Space
Between Us.

00:01:10.109 --> 00:01:15.469
So I watched the short film, which is written
and directed by Dutch filmmaker Marc S Noellkaemper,

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:19.130
and I have to say, if this is plagiarism,
they didn’t try to hide it.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.310
The main character is a cleaning lady at some
kind of secret lab facility.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.929
The Space Between us is about this post-war
era where oxygen is scarce and people want

00:01:27.929 --> 00:01:30.909
gills so they can take advantage of the oxygen
underwater.

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:35.319
So these scientists are developing this fish
person so they can give it’s gills to their

00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:38.990
leader, or whoever this person is.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.709
Whereas in the Shape of Water, scientists
are developing the fishman as some kind of

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:44.329
weapon for the Cold War.

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:48.000
The place where the subjects are stored is
a high security area.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.409
They are stored in these vertical water tanks
with glass windows and the people in charge

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:54.261
seem to have sinister plans for their specimen.

00:01:54.261 --> 00:01:58.999
The fishmen themselves are blue and black
humanoid creatures.

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:03.569
The one in the Shape of Water has webbed feet,
while this one has a more traditional mermaid

00:02:03.569 --> 00:02:04.569
tail.

00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:08.060
They don’t like being locked up and the
main girl sets them free and sneaks them out

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.060
of the facility.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.390
The cinematography is similar.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.640
The sound design is similar from what we can
tell so far.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.750
Even some of the shots seem to be almost identical.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.459
So did Guillermo Del Toro rip off this film?

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:23.200
Maybe, but I don’t think there’s enough
information to convict him.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.310
Del Toro claims to have been developing the
film since 2011, which means nothing I mean

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.840
be could be trying to cover up his plagiarism
with that statement, but it does take at least

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.129
a couple years to develop a complex feature
film like this.

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:38.780
The Space Between Us was successfully crowdfunded
in August 2015, but it was first announced

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:39.780
in late 2014.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.511
But the strange thing is, while the indie
film community has raised this issue, the

00:02:43.511 --> 00:02:46.760
director, Marc Noellkaemper has been silent
on it.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.210
He doesn't exactly have much social media
presence, but they do have a website and Facebook

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.540
page for the film and the similarities with
The Shape of Water have not been brought up.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:03:00.040
There haven’t been any writing credits signalling
that The Shape of Water is based on The Space

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.040
Between Us.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.080
The only person from either film who has even
acknowledged this, is the production designer

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:09.680
from the indie film, who just says that Del
Toro’s picture seems to be inspired by their

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.680
short.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.400
He doesn’t seem mad about it even, just
kind of proud of it I guess.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.430
There could be a contract going on behind
the scenes so until the director comes out

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.819
and cries foul, I don’t see how I can get
too upset about it.

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:23.420
Definitely suspicious how similar these films
are though.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.000
But there’s one more possible connection.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.019
I was sceptical about it at first, but the
commenters have raised some good points.

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:34.689
I asked in the previous video about the significance
of the shoes that they keep putting emphasis

00:03:34.689 --> 00:03:38.840
on in the trailer and some of you thought
it might be a reference to The Little Mermaid,

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.760
only the roles would be reversed to where
the male is the fish person instead.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.840
In the trailer, she’s referred to as “the
princess without a voice”, just as Ariel

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.650
gives up her voice in The Little Mermaid to
go on land.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:54.340
The significance of her giving up her shoes
could her giving up her former life on land

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.520
to go be with the fish person underwater.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:00.890
James Heskett points out that her shoe falls
off during the scene where she kisses or dreams

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.849
of kissing the fishman representing her letting
go of her ties to her life on land to find

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:07.829
her love below the surface.

00:04:07.829 --> 00:04:12.590
Skyler has another idea about the shoe symbol,
explaining that the zodiac sign Pisces is

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:13.780
the sign of the fish.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.680
Pisces rules the feet, so the shoes will probably
symbolically tie into that.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.360
Pisces is known as being a sign of dreams
and escapism, among other things.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:28.030
He wasn’t the only one to point out instances
of symbolism that I missed in the trailer.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:31.220
Brendan Ramos suggested that the fact the
she’s a cleaning lady could have something

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.699
to do with her clearing the evidence after
she steals and hides the specimen later in

00:04:35.699 --> 00:04:36.699
the film.

00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:40.670
Maybe some of the evidence she cleans up could
be this blood handprint on the theater.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:44.550
I talked about this possibly being from the
creature attacking someone and getting blood

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.889
on his hands, but it’s also been suggested
it could come from Shannon, since we see his

00:04:48.889 --> 00:04:50.890
hand wrapped up in another shot.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.669
I still think it’s more likely a handprint
from the creature since it is stated that

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:57.960
he’s a dangerous animal, but that’s really
just my gut feeling.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.360
I also talked about the bathtub and the tub
of aviex, but Mitchel Baldwin points out that

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:06.500
there’s a strange substance in the tub floating
around and the same can be seen in the creature’s

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.340
tank at the lab.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.550
My guess is that it’s some kind of solution
that helps the creature in some way, so when

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:17.240
Eliza sneaks the creature out the lab, she
also steals that solution so that the fishman

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:21.210
can survive in her tub until she figures out
a better solution for him.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.680
There were a couple of things I got wrong
in my other video, like when I said this could

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.009
be a tentacle of some kind.

00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:29.880
Looking at the other shots in the sequence,
it makes more sense that this is just a curtain

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.539
or blanket in the room.

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:37.139
I also said that the voice could be Doug Jones,
but I wasn’t really sure.

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:44.270
It seems that it’s actually Richard Jenkins,
who may play a father figure to Elisa.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:48.569
And then there’s the song, which I brought
up as something in style of classical music,

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:52.849
which was another piece of evidence toward
this fishman being related to Abe Sapien,

00:05:52.849 --> 00:05:54.590
I’ll touch more on that later.

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:58.250
But what I had said was that this movie was
pulling a Baz Luhrmann because the recording

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.800
was actually released in ‘06.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.270
What I didn’t realize, what that this version
was actually a cover.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:07.470
The song has been covered forever throughout
history, so it actually fits just fine in

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.370
a historical context.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:13.780
I predicted that some of the scenes in the
trailer may actually be dreams, and this girl

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:18.860
took it a step further by saying that if the
subject does really have those psychic abilities,

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:23.050
he may be the one causing Elisa to have these
dreams with his powers.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:27.080
And speaking of powers, many of you brought
up this scene in the trailer where Elisa looks

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.560
to be controlling some water droplets on the
window.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:33.979
I didn’t think much of it before, because
I assumed she was in the lab, the camera right

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:38.229
here is inside the water tank, and those were
just some bubbles she was pointing to.

00:06:38.229 --> 00:06:42.100
It wasn’t until I saw a comment referring
to this as “the bus window scene”, when

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.520
I noticed that she is in fact inside of a
vehicle, as evidenced by the reflection of

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.900
a traffic light.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.530
So she is actually controlling these raindrops
with some kind of telekinetic power, perhaps

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:56.729
something she learned from the creature and
definitely more evidence that a psychic connection

00:06:56.729 --> 00:07:01.970
does exist in this movie, and with that, it’s
impossible not to think about Abe Sapien.

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:05.810
Let’s just for a moment set aside our views
on if this creature is related to Hellboy

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:09.590
in way and give him the benefit of the doubt
for a moment.

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:13.759
There are obviously some differences in the
design of Abe Sapien from Hellboy 1 and 2

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:15.720
compared to The Shape of Water creature.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:20.120
But one person pointed out that this new creature
could actually be based on the design from

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:25.180
the BPRD Hell on Earth comics, which look
much more similar to The Shape of Water’s

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.180
monster.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:30.349
This guy on the other hand, mentions the new
creature is BLUE, just like Del Toro.

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:35.530
Wow, PitSniper, you know... I never noticed
that before but Guillermo actually is blue

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.530
isn’t he?

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.409
I’m so glad you pointed that out -- okay
I’m done.

00:07:39.409 --> 00:07:40.530
I’m absolutely done.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:44.819
But on a more serious note, maybe this man
near the end of the trailer is a recast of

00:07:44.819 --> 00:07:46.879
Professor Broom.

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:50.310
Probably the most popular comment that I got
though, were the comments about Eliza and

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:54.990
the fishman creature being Abe Sapiens parents
or Grandparents, and I think it’s reasonable

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:59.150
say that this creature is of the same species
as Abe, but if you look at the timeline of

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:03.400
events there’s no way that Abe is their
descendent, because Abe had already been discovered

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.900
about 100 years before the events of The Shape
of Water take place.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.560
Some of you also discussed that Fox Searchlight
probably doesn’t have the rights to make

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.740
a new Hellboy movie and I think this comment
perfectly sums up my views on the subject.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:19.560
Referring to an interview with Guillermo years
ago, he did state that the fantasy world in

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.050
his films does loosely have a connection.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:26.310
Legally, he wouldn’t be able to make a Hellboy
flick, but from an artistic point of view,

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.639
he could make a movie closely resembling the
characters in the Hellboy franchise, as many

00:08:30.639 --> 00:08:33.079
movies have done and gotten away with.

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:37.950
In that scenario, he could albeit make every
little detail point towards being a prequel

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.219
without actually saying that it is.

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:45.050
As long as they don’t explicitly state any
names, locations or details, he could imply

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:46.180
a loose connection.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:50.190
If this is the case, that would explain why
Guillermo Del Toro and Doug Jones have to

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:54.170
deny any connection to the Hellboy universe
in interviews, especially with a new Hellboy

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.540
reboot on the horizon.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.510
And I think that’s as much as we’ll see
in the Shape of Water.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:02.450
This creature is just another organism from
the same species as Abe.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:06.680
The title of the movie is a perfect analogy
for the relationship it has to Hellboy.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:10.990
The film is called The Shape of Water, but
water molecules are fluid, they don’t actually

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:12.490
have any one defined shape.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.560
The movie won’t be shaped as a Hellboy movie.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:18.380
It won’t have any of those characters, names
or plot points.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:23.700
But this will just be it’s own movie, composed
of the familiar materials that make up Abe

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:24.700
Sapien.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:27.340
They’ll just be taking on a new shape.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:31.700
Scary story narrations are also taking on
a new shape, in the new True Horror Game for

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.810
mobile phones.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:36.910
My friend and fellow narrator Let’s Read
just launched his game for Android and iOS

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.829
that lets you choose your own horror adventure.

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:41.251
It comes with 10 stories and is totally ad
free.

00:09:41.251 --> 00:09:44.350
I’ll leave a link to the download in the
description.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.350
Next week The Shape of Water comes out and
you’ll definitely want to see my Things

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.740
You Missed where I’ll be going into detail
on it, so remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:56.250
for new horrors every week, ring that deathbell
for notifications and I’ll see you in the

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.270
next one.

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:59.050
Assuming we both survive.

